{"repositoryId":1276962100,"availability":"available","full":"CODERUDRA-X/AEGIS-SWARM","name":"AEGIS-SWARM","description":"Consensus-driven multi-agent emergency intelligence system using computer vision, real MCP protocol, and iterative AI reasoning for trusted operational decision-making.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":19,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-22T13:03:29Z","updated":"2026-10-13T17:13:44Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://aegis-swarm-tan.vercel.app","topics":["agentic-swarm","ai-agents","computer-vision","decision-intelligence-systems","emergency-response","multi-agent-system"],"demo":"https://aegis-swarm-tan.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:32.961Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:32.961Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:32.961Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T03:00:32.961Z","stars":19,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The AI That Refuses to Trust Its First Answer.","Crowd crushes are predictable. Kanjuruhan. Itaewon. Astroworld. They happen because no one trusted the data fast enough.","Current crowd monitoring is reactive — a human watches a screen, notices a problem too late, and acts too slowly. AEGIS-SWARM makes the pipeline autonomous, multi-perspective, and consensus-gated: no action is taken until independent AI agents agree."],"features":["👁️ Observed — Scout extracts spatial facts directly from raw pixels","🧠 Analyzed — Risk Agent classifies threat level from structured data","📡 Verified — Independent MCP evidence (venue occupancy/exits, weather) is gathered — not just visual guesswork","⚔️ Challenged — Critic Agent independently contests the assessment, weighing that evidence, and classifies it as supporting / contradicting / insufficient / unavailable","🔁 Debated — If Critic disagrees, Risk re-evaluates with Critic's feedback (iterative loop)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CODERUDRA-X/AEGIS-SWARM/